The `TS_NANOSECS_()` method returns nanoseconds since the last system cold-load while `JULIANTIMESTAMP()` returns microseconds since about the creation of the world in biblical tradition. The two are independent. I get that this is hard to certify. There is no explicit hardware randomizer, so doing this based on what is in `rand_unix.c` seems closer to that.

In any event, the current pull request only applies to the x86 platform, and I'll keep it that way.

